  "notes": "West leads the ♥Q against 6♠. Assuming trumps can be played without loss, South still has a potential loser in both diamonds and clubs. There are finessing positions in both of those suits and dummy's fourth diamond may provide a discard for the ♣Q.\n\nSouth can in fact virtually guarantee his contract. After winning the heart lead, South cashes another heart trick. Next South cashes dummy's ♠A and ♠K, unblocking high spades from the closed hand. When both defenders follow the contract is certain.\n\nSouth ruffs dummy's last heart high, eliminating that suit, then crosses to dummy in spades and leads a low diamond covering whatever East plays. West can win the trick, but he will be endplayed.\n\nA heart return yields a ruff and discard. A return of either diamonds or clubs gives South his twelfth trick as well. Notice the importance of unblocking the spades. On a diamond return from West, South may need a dummy entry to be able to cash all 3 diamond tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥Q against 6♠. Assuming trumps can be played without loss, South still has a potential loser in both diamonds and clubs. There are finessing positions in both of those suits and dummy's fourth diamond may provide a discard for the ♣Q.",
    "South can in fact virtually guarantee his contract. After winning the heart lead, South cashes another heart trick. Next South cashes dummy's ♠A and ♠K, unblocking high spades from the closed hand. When both defenders follow the contract is certain.",
    "South ruffs dummy's last heart high, eliminating that suit, then crosses to dummy in spades and leads a low diamond covering whatever East plays. West can win the trick, but he will be endplayed.",
    "A heart return yields a ruff and discard. A return of either diamonds or clubs gives South his twelfth trick as well. Notice the importance of unblocking the spades. On a diamond return from West, South may need a dummy entry to be able to cash all 3 diamond tricks."
  ],
